# --- Build output -----------------------------------------------------------
# All rebuildable, and far too large for a repo.
build/
dist/
installer_output/
*.spec.bak

# --- Bundled ffmpeg ---------------------------------------------------------
# IMPORTANT: ffmpeg.exe and ffprobe.exe are roughly 127 MB each, which is over
# GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit. Committing them gets the push rejected, and
# removing them from history afterwards is genuinely painful. They're fetched
# on demand by:  build.py --with-ffmpeg
vendor/

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Editors and OS ---------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- Runtime ----------------------------------------------------------------
# The downloaded-video archive, if anyone ever points a download at the repo.
.clipstash-archive.txt

# --- NOT ignored, deliberately ----------------------------------------------
# assets/*.ico, *.png, *.icns and *.bmp ARE committed, even though they're
# generated. Regenerating them needs cairosvg, which usually can't be installed
# on Windows because it depends on Cairo's DLLs. Keeping the rendered files in
# the repo means a Windows checkout can build without it. They total under 3 MB.
